{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md | tail -n 28; rg -n 'R06|R12|C5|A1' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round55-brief.md\"","aggregated_output":"    62\t    so it is not the market's reference.\n    63\t  - **The Claude adjudicator's view:** the rule allows a figure computed only from consensus, guidance and reported figures.\n    64\t  - The original design took the Claude view: DESIGN.md C5 passes q02's \"$392B consensus × 92% reported mix\" as a reference.\n    65\t- **A label that changes the quantity (R09, S's Claude writer).** Company-wide capex was labelled \"data-center capex\".\n    66\t  - The Codex adjudicator calls it not supported (an outcome not of the question's quantity).\n    67\t  - The Claude adjudicator calls it supported: the passages use the two terms interchangeably (e5376 against e5081).\n    68\t\n    69\t**Support.** Every forecast is supported by both adjudicators, except R09, where the families split as above.\n    70\t\n    71\t## 3. What the test shows\n    72\t\n    73\t- **The request now states its rules.**\n    74\t  - Twelve first answers from two writer families produced no schema refusal and no refusal on an unstated rule.\n    75\t  - The one code refusal was a checker error.\n    76\t  - Compare the paid gate (D733), where 0 of 90 outcomes named a figure.\n    77\t- **The checker still holds one error of mine:** the \"from … to …\" range.\n    78\t- **The indirect route through an estimate's `rests_on` let one real inconsistency through.** D738 chose to record such routes for\n    79\t  readers. The readers caught it, and the registered stop rule counts their catch.\n    80\t- **The two reader families apply different thresholds** to a computed market reference and to a relabelled quantity. These are ruler\n    81\t  questions. By the council-loop rule \"Model readers carry their family's threshold … take a balanced set of boundary cases to Alex;\n    82\t  his rulings are the ruler\", they go to Alex.\n    83\t- **The joint and separate answers in P agree closely.** v4 is 416–420 and v8 385–387, all rung 2. This is one draw each, a strong\n    84\t  writer, and not gpt-6-luna. It is no evidence for D725's joint-versus-separate question.\n    85\t\n    86\t## 4. Not measured\n    87\t\n    88\tWhether gpt-6-luna at medium effort follows the format: only the paid re-send measures that. Readers' quality judgements beyond the\n    89\tfive defects were not graded.\n23:   - (b) The R06 two-forecast defect. Both readers and both adjudicators upheld it, yet both adjudicators rejected R12's claim, and R12\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py | sed -n '1,41p;111,158p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py | sed -n '747,798p'; rg -n 'reference.*estimate|one forecast figure|a complete number' poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/P-v4/schema.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
