{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py | sed -n '15,25p'; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/CHECKED.json | sed -n '209,260p;565,580p'; rg -n 'D726|proxy clause|total capex' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -n 21\"","aggregated_output":"    15\tSCALE = {'trillion': 1000.0, 'tn': 1000.0, 't': 1000.0, 'billion': 1.0, 'bn': 1.0, 'b': 1.0, 'million': 0.001, 'm': 0.001}\n    16\tNUM = r'(\\d[\\d,]*(?:\\.\\d+)?)'\n    17\tUNIT = r'(trillion|billion|million|bn|tn|T|B|M)\\b'\n    18\tQWORDS = '|'.join(sorted(QUAL, key=len, reverse=True))\n    19\tPATTERNS = [\n    20\t    ('relative', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT + r',?\\s*(?:plus or minus|±)\\s*' + NUM + r'%')),\n    21\t    ('range', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*(?:' + UNIT + r')?\\s*(?:–|-)\\s*\\$?\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT)),   # \"to\" is ambiguous (\"from $253 billion to $392 billion\")\n    22\t    ('range', re.compile(r'\\bbetween\\s+\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*(?:' + UNIT + r')?\\s+and\\s+\\$?\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT, re.I)),\n    23\t    ('qualified', re.compile(r'\\b(' + QWORDS + r')\\s+\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT, re.I)),\n    24\t    ('money', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT)),\n    25\t    ('money_plain', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'(?![\\d,.]*\\s*(?:trillion|billion|million|bn|tn|T|B|M)\\b)')),\n   209\t  \"case\": \"P-v4\",\n   210\t  \"writer\": \"codex\",\n   211\t  \"sha256\": \"4178eb13324854838b3e093777c3a8393da265f15182bf429abb5ec99317039c\",\n   212\t  \"stage\": \"checked\",\n   213\t  \"errors\": [],\n   214\t  \"recorded\": [\n   215\t   {\n   216\t    \"type\": \"qualified source\",\n   217\t    \"figure\": \"F5\",\n   218\t    \"qualifier\": \"roughly\"\n   219\t   },\n   220\t   {\n   221\t    \"type\": \"estimate\",\n   222\t    \"figure\": \"F6\",\n   223\t    \"assumption\": \"I expect a beat in line with the independent estimate based on past guidance beats. The prior quarter's beat, Vera Rubin production shipments and CoreWeave's live deployment support that estimate. I keep the China Data Center compute assumption at zero for this quarter.\"\n   224\t   },\n   225\t   {\n   226\t    \"type\": \"conversion between quantities\",\n   227\t    \"figure\": \"F7\"\n   228\t   },\n   229\t   {\n   230\t    \"type\": \"estimate\",\n   231\t    \"figure\": \"F8\",\n   232\t    \"assumption\": \"I carry forward the sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance and allow a modest increase as Rubin supply expands and hyperscaler sales reaccelerate. Memory, power and long delivery lead times limit how much demand can ship this quarter. The estimate allows a small contribution from limited H200 sales if China authorizes purchases in time.\"\n   233\t   },\n   234\t   {\n   235\t    \"type\": \"carried across periods\",\n   236\t    \"figure\": \"F9\"\n   237\t   },\n   238\t   {\n   239\t    \"type\": \"one quantity, several figures\",\n   240\t    \"figure\": \"F4\",\n   241\t    \"figures\": [\n   242\t     \"F4\",\n   243\t     \"F5\",\n   244\t     \"F6\"\n   245\t    ],\n   246\t    \"what\": [\n   247\t     \"NVIDIA\",\n   248\t     \"revenue\",\n   249\t     \"company\",\n   250\t     \"FY2027 Q3\"\n   251\t    ]\n   252\t   }\n   253\t  ],\n   254\t  \"published\": {\n   255\t   \"v4\": [\n   256\t    419.808,\n   257\t    419.808,\n   258\t    null\n   259\t   ]\n   260\t  },\n   565\t },\n   566\t {\n   567\t  \"case\": \"E\",\n   568\t  \"writer\": \"claude\",\n   569\t  \"sha256\": \"1e1a5cccf453c9d064bcf533e853dd83fa0073a9dbdca8576698cacfdbed6649\",\n   570\t  \"stage\": \"checked\",\n   571\t  \"errors\": [\n   572\t   [\n   573\t    \"S1\",\n   574\t    \"F4: \\\"$35 billion\\\" is part of the longer expression \\\"$35 billion to $170 billion\\\" in e4857; copy it whole\"\n   575\t   ]\n   576\t  ],\n   577\t  \"recorded\": [],\n   578\t  \"published\": {},\n   579\t  \"decision\": \"refused\"\n   580\t },\n2554:- The class ($0, `docs/research/2026-10-27-shared-quantity/proof.py`): every AI-capex aggregate candidate of r3, r4 and r5 (9, 11, 11) against the theses that existed before it. r3 (no collision judge) opened six 2026 aggregates; r4 and r5, with the judge, each opened one duplicate: the judge read \"Big Tech AI outlays\" against \"the top five's total capex\" (r4 seq 351) and \"the five named companies' capex\" against \"industrywide AI infrastructure spending\" (r5 seq 200) as distinct questions in one matter, and later candidates then merged into the duplicate (r4: two). The contract already says what identity is: `industry_aggregate` is \"one aggregate quantity for one calendar year … another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\" (role-v12), and D155 puts identity in code where it is fully determined.\n10102:## D680 · 2026-11-19 · Merge test closed (council e): delivery verified, the registered test did not pass (P2's proxy clause and V missed)\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
