{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11122,11140p'; rg --files --no-ignore poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22 | head -n 35; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\s*\\\"[A-Za-z_]+\\\":' poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/results.json | head -n 20\"","aggregated_output":" 11122\t## D733 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid gate: STOP, every answer refused; the format's rules were never stated in the request (council round 48); repair or close is Alex's choice\n 11123\t\n 11124\t- **What ran** (D732): 36 scored first attempts and 36 diagnostic retries, gpt-6-luna, $0.3677 of $0.50 (ledger: 72 attempts,\n 11125\t  not stopped). Run folder `poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`. Record: `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`.\n 11126\t- **Registered result (D725's lines, scored as written, D680):** all 72 answers refused by `calc_check.py`, none published; the joint\n 11127\t  arm is usable in 0 of 9 pairs (needs 8). **STOP.** Complete, not INCOMPLETE: every attempt finished. The blind reading was not run:\n 11128\t  its brief says a card with no answer cannot be usable, and every card has none.\n 11129\t- **What it measures:** not D725's question (whether one call over a family gives better numbers), only that the answer format, as\n 11130\t  the request stated it, could not be filled.\n 11131\t- **Census (council round 48; Codex reproduced every refusal):**\n 11132\t  - 0 of 90 member answers named a figure as the outcome; the model wrote the number in words (\"$398.1 billion\");\n 11133\t  - prose where an id is expected, first attempts: `reference.figure` 39, `evidence` 175 (139 on source figures), `bridge` 49;\n 11134\t  - 52 figures gave both a value and a range;\n 11135\t  - the structure check stopped 63 of 72 answers before any source or arithmetic check.\n 11136\t- **Mechanism:**\n 11137\t  - The format's rules live in the check, not in the request. The sent schema has 7 field descriptions. `evidence`, `outcome`,\n 11138\t    `unit`, `value`/`low`/`high`, `inputs`, `operation`, `signs` and ten more have none.\n 11139\t  - The descriptions of `bridge` and `reference` read as asking for prose, while the check reads ids.\n 11140\t  - Under that layer, checks refuse right answers:\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/ledger.lock\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/gate.launcher.lock\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/ledger.attempts.jsonl\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/ledger.json\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/answers.jsonl\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/retries.jsonl\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/plan.json\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/results.json\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-3-separate-v3-d1-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-separate-v8-d3-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/single-O-single-d1-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-joint-d3-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-2-joint-d1-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-separate-v4-d2-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-2-separate-v9-d1-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/single-S-single-d2-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-2-separate-v14-d3-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-3-separate-v35-d3-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/single-O-single-d3-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-separate-v8-d1-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-3-separate-v3-d3-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/single-E-single-d2-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-joint-d1-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-2-separate-v9-d3-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-2-separate-v14-d1-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-2-joint-d3-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-3-joint-d2-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-3-separate-v35-d1-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-separate-v8-d2-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/single-E-single-d1-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-joint-d2-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/single-S-single-d3-a2.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-2-separate-v14-d2-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-3-joint-d1-a1.sqlite\npoc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/archives/pair-old-1-separate-v4-d3-a2.sqlite\n2: \"finals\": {\n4:   \"status\": \"answered\",\n5:   \"data\": {\n6:    \"figures\": [\n8:      \"id\": \"fy2026_total\",\n9:      \"what\": {\n10:       \"population\": \"NVIDIA\",\n11:       \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n12:       \"scope\": \"company\",\n13:       \"period\": \"FY2026\"\n15:      \"basis\": \"reported\",\n16:      \"scenario\": \"actual\",\n17:      \"kind\": \"source\",\n18:      \"value\": 215.9,\n19:      \"low\": null,\n20:      \"high\": null,\n21:      \"bound\": null,\n22:      \"unit\": \"$ billion\",\n23:      \"evidence\": \"e4273\",\n24:      \"expression\": \"$215.9 billion\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
