{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10065,10131p'; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/S/answers/codex.json | sed -n '145,192p'; rg -n 'e2295' poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/P/user.txt | cut -c 1-450\"","aggregated_output":" 10065\t- **Council:** Claude's proposal (written first), Codex's cold independent design and one challenge round, which ended in consensus.\n 10066\t- **The design:** `docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/MERGE-PLAN.md`.\n 10067\t  - Opening and answer choices come from the old system, and a refused proposal stays out of the open list.\n 10068\t  - Reading, earlier versions, repeats and unlinked facts come from clean Steps 1–3.\n 10069\t  - Judging stays the frozen judge.\n 10070\t  - NVIDIA's own figures follow D382/D505 unless Alex makes an exception. The ceilings are 6 and 10 of 32.\n 10071\t  - The main risk is meaning drift.\n 10072\t- **The test:**\n 10073\t  - 11 frozen articles for M04 and M17, plus 1 control, against old-2's and old-3's question lists;\n 10074\t  - 4 judge answers, blind-read;\n 10075\t  - 5 pass lines, written beforehand;\n 10076\t  - $0.33–0.42.\n 10077\t  - It waits for Alex's approval, since D677 holds paid sends.\n 10078\t\n 10079\t## D679 · 2026-11-19 · Alex lifts D677's paid-send stop for the merge test only; the test runs on 70 articles, two old draws, two judging arms, under a $5 ledger\n 10080\t\n 10081\t- **Alex (the session goal):** \"write the plan, execute the plan, and don't do full blown runs, validate it works based on metrics we\n 10082\t  meassure for quality\".\n 10083\t- **The plan:** `docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/EXECUTION-PLAN.md`, revised by council rounds c and d (`council-c-codex.md`,\n 10084\t  `council-d-codex.md`).\n 10085\t- **The article set.** It became the 70 window articles that either system tied to M04 and M17, plus the census and the control.\n 10086\t  - My first count read the census numbers as positions in `kept-articles.json`. They are numbers in `census/numbering.json`. Codex\n 10087\t    caught it.\n 10088\t  - The same misreading put custom-chip and DRAM theses into a first list of 126.\n 10089\t- **Per-article open lists** were agreed in round d: the old questions open when the article was read.\n 10090\t- **The judging copy.** A 09-06 cutoff copy of each old store, with the frozen judge restricted to the target questions on one daily\n 10091\t  schedule for both arms (hybrid: c8's filing; control: old's own evidence).\n 10092\t- **Checks before any send ($0):**\n 10093\t  - c8's request, rebuilt, equals the stored c8 request byte for byte.\n 10094\t  - The control arm, answered with old's archived answers on old's schedule, rebuilt 25 of 25 capex requests byte for byte, and all 22\n 10095\t    Anthropic requests with the same evidence. Their only difference is the theme block: other questions held at 09-06.\n 10096\t- **Lines** P1, P2, P3 and P5 hold in both draws, plus a validity line V; P4 is diagnostic only.\n 10097\t- **Ceiling:** $5 on a new ledger. The estimate is about $1.4 for c8 and about $0.2 for judging. This is within D439's $40.\n 10098\t- **Also recorded:** PATH-TO-PASS's census C named new-2's clean-26 and clean-7, and new-3's clean-29, clean-6 and clean-12, as capex\n 10099\t  theses. They are custom-chip and memory theses, so census C's capex reading is to be re-checked before it is relied on.\n 10100\t\n 10101\t\n 10102\t## D680 · 2026-11-19 · Merge test closed (council e): delivery verified, the registered test did not pass (P2's proxy clause and V missed)\n 10103\t\n 10104\t- **Ran under D679**, for $2.13 of a $5 ledger: 140 c8 sends, 98 judge calls in two arms, 15 noise re-sends, and two blind reader\n 10105\t  families on 20 cards with 5 controls.\n 10106\t- **Held:**\n 10107\t  - P1, delivery, 4/4: the hybrid's final requests carry c8's four-company $720–745B item and the Reuters anchor-talks items;\n 10108\t  - P3, talks stay talks, 2/2;\n 10109\t  - P5, both readers support all 4 hybrid answers, settled in round 0;\n 10110\t  - P4 (diagnostic): 0 NVIDIA-figure proposals of 7;\n 10111\t  - the reader controls: 3 plants unsupported, 2 controls supported.\n 10112\t- **Missed:**\n 10113\t  - **P2's second clause.** Total capex is used for data-center capex without being named a proxy; old misses it the same way.\n 10114\t  - **V.** The control's v47 was unsupported. Its 09-16 request, re-sent, gave rungs 2, 1, 2 against old's 2, 2, 2. The requests differ in\n 10115\t    the theme block and the previous wording, so a reconstruction effect is not ruled out.\n 10116\t- **What the answers rest on.** Capex rests partly on 09-06 history: 26–27 c8 items against 16–20 history items in the final requests.\n 10117\t  The Anthropic answers rest wholly on c8's filing.\n 10118\t- **Errors of mine** (caught by Codex):\n 10119\t  - the census numbering misread;\n 10120\t  - a first article list with off-matter theses;\n 10121\t  - a judging copy refused by the store's append-only triggers.\n 10122\t- **Closed with no further sends.** The next step is Alex's.\n 10123\t- Record: `docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md`, `council-e-codex.md`.\n 10124\t\n 10125\t## D681 · 2026-11-20 · Alex opens the hybrid system's build and test; phase 1 is a new judge version (J2) for the judge's reasoning errors\n 10126\t\n 10127\t- Alex, 2026-11-20, after the merge test (D680) and the finding that the old system loses on the 32 matters at opening and in the judge's\n 10128\t  reasoning, not in reading: \"不是聊了半天就是要合并两边最好的来提升系统吗？\"; then, on the proposal to fix the judge's reasoning errors\n 10129\t  first as a new judge version, with a council review and a test of a few cents: \"可以啊，你现在开始做hybrid system 的构建和测试，不要犯了和做新系统一样的错误到最后才发现问题\".\n 10130\t- Decided (his words): the hybrid system is built and tested. The judge (judging-v7, frozen by D354) may get a new version, J2, measured\n 10131\t  against v7. The frozen ruler is unchanged.\n   145\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   146\t    },\n   147\t    {\n   148\t      \"id\": \"F7\",\n   149\t      \"what\": {\n   150\t        \"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   151\t        \"measure\": \"capital spending outside the data-center forecast\",\n   152\t        \"scope\": \"combined non-data-center spending and net data-center spending deferred beyond CY2026\",\n   153\t        \"period\": \"CY2026\"\n   154\t      },\n   155\t      \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n   156\t      \"basis\": \"forecast\",\n   157\t      \"value\": 30,\n   158\t      \"low\": null,\n   159\t      \"high\": null,\n   160\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   161\t      \"evidence_id\": null,\n   162\t      \"quote_number\": null,\n   163\t      \"qualifier\": null,\n   164\t      \"inputs\": null,\n   165\t      \"operation\": null,\n   166\t      \"basis_text\": \"I estimate a modest deduction from company-wide plans, mostly for capital spending outside data centers, including Amazon's retail operations, with a smaller allowance for project delays. The four companies' AI infrastructure indication and the proximity of Meta's AI spending estimate to its total guidance support treating data centers as the dominant use of capital. The delay tally covers a broader pool of projects and their full project values, so I allow only for the portion likely to displace spending by these companies this year.\",\n   167\t      \"rests_on\": [\"F1\", \"F2\", \"F5\", \"F6\", \"e122\", \"e5292\"],\n   168\t      \"outcome_for\": [],\n   169\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   170\t    },\n   171\t    {\n   172\t      \"id\": \"F8\",\n   173\t      \"what\": {\n   174\t        \"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   175\t        \"measure\": \"data-center capex\",\n   176\t        \"scope\": \"combined\",\n   177\t        \"period\": \"CY2026\"\n   178\t      },\n   179\t      \"kind\": \"computed\",\n   180\t      \"basis\": \"forecast\",\n   181\t      \"value\": 715,\n   182\t      \"low\": null,\n   183\t      \"high\": null,\n   184\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   185\t      \"evidence_id\": null,\n   186\t      \"quote_number\": null,\n   187\t      \"qualifier\": null,\n   188\t      \"inputs\": [\"F2\", \"F7\"],\n   189\t      \"operation\": \"difference\",\n   190\t      \"basis_text\": null,\n   191\t      \"rests_on\": null,\n   192\t      \"outcome_for\": [\"v6\"],\n591:- e2295 [third_party_view; Morningstar (analyst); original source Morningstar 2026-08-19; from gnews:7ce47efd62fa17b9aa29e258 2026-08-19] Morningstar cites NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $3 billion in FY2020 and $194 billion in FY2026, and estimates $361 billion in FY2027, up 86% year over year.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,96p'; rg -n 'def .*scan|0 of 90|0/90|member answers named' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers -g '*.py' -g '*.md' | head -n 30\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13 paid gate: result (D733)\n     2\t\n     3\t**STOP.** Every one of the 72 answers was refused by the code checks: 36 scored first attempts and 36 diagnostic retries. Nothing\n     4\twas published, and the joint arm is usable in 0 of 9 pairs against the registered 8 of 9.\n     5\t\n     6\tThe result does not answer the question the gate was built for: does judging related number questions in one call give better\n     7\tnumbers than judging each alone? It shows that the answer format, as the request stated it, could not be filled. Most refusals are\n     8\trules the request never stated, or checks that refuse right answers. A few are the model's own errors.\n     9\t\n    10\t- **Run:** `poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`, sent once (D732) with gpt-6-luna. The ledger records 72 attempts and\n    11\t  $0.3677 of the $0.50 ceiling: $0.1554 for the first attempts and $0.2124 for the retries. Every attempt finished with status\n    12\t  `answered`, so the result is complete, not INCOMPLETE.\n    13\t- **The blind reading** was not run. The registered brief says \"A card that has no answer cannot be usable\", and every card has\n    14\t  none, so the readers cannot change the verdict.\n    15\t- **Council round 48:**\n    16\t  - `round48-brief.md`;\n    17\t  - `claude-r48.md`, Claude's reflection, written first;\n    18\t  - `codex-r48.md`, an independent fresh read-only Codex session that reproduced every refusal from the journals and the requests.\n    19\t\n    20\t## 1. Census (first attempt → retry; Codex's count, which corrects Claude's)\n    21\t\n    22\t| Attempt | Arm | Answers | Structure (C7) messages / answers | Stopped at the structure check |\n    23\t|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n    24\t| First | Joint | 9 | 39 / 9 | 9 |\n    25\t| First | Separate | 18 | 47 / 18 | 17 |\n    26\t| First | Single | 9 | 13 / 9 | 8 |\n    27\t| Retry | Joint | 9 | 40 / 9 | 9 |\n    28\t| Retry | Separate | 18 | 41 / 18 | 14 |\n    29\t| Retry | Single | 9 | 12 / 9 | 6 |\n    30\t\n    31\t`check()` returns early after any structure error, so most source, arithmetic and compatibility checks never ran on these answers.\n    32\t\n    33\t**Prose where the check expects an id**, counted by occurrence:\n    34\t\n    35\t| Field | First | Retry |\n    36\t|---|---:|---:|\n    37\t| `answers[].outcome` | 45 of 45 | 45 of 45 |\n    38\t| `answers[].reference.figure` | 39 | 32 |\n    39\t| `figures[].evidence` (139 of them on source figures, where C1 needs a passage id) | 175 | 133 (95) |\n    40\t| `figures[].bridge` | 49 | 44 |\n    41\t| `converts`, `disputed`, `inputs` | 3 | 3 |\n    42\t\n    43\t**Not one of the 90 member answers named a figure as its outcome**, in either journal. This failure alone refuses every answer.\n    44\tThe retries did not repair it. They carried the first attempt's reasons, and the early return had hidden this reason on most\n    45\tanswers.\n    46\t\n    47\t## 2. Mechanism\n    48\t\n    49\t1. **The format's rules live in `calc_check.py`, not in the request.**\n    50\t   - The sent schema carries 7 descriptions: `what`, `basis`, `kind`, `expression`, `relation`, `bridge` and `reference`.\n    51\t   - These fields have none: `value`, `low`, `high`, `bound`, `unit`, `evidence`, `component`, `inputs`, `operation`, `signs`,\n    52\t     `disputed`, `basis_text`, `rests_on`, `converts`, `scenario`, `outcome` and `rung`.\n    53\t   - The check enforces closed conventions on them:\n    54\t     - ids, not prose, in `evidence`, `outcome`, `reference.figure`, `bridge` and `disputed`;\n    55\t     - the unit spellings `USD bn`, `%` and `x`;\n    56\t     - a value or a range, never both (all 52 such refusals gave both);\n    57\t     - the period label `H1`;\n    58\t     - `share`, not `product`, for a percentage;\n    59\t     - each operation's operand count;\n    60\t     - `signs` only on `sum` and `roll_forward`.\n    61\t   - The descriptions of `bridge` (\"an estimate stating the conversion …\") and `reference` (\"An external figure, or a calculation …\")\n    62\t     read as asking for prose. The check reads both as ids.\n    63\t   - REQUEST-AUDIT.md says \"field definitions moved to the schema\". Most did not reach the sent bytes.\n    64\t2. **Some checks refuse right answers.** Each case was exposed by replaying a stored answer with the earlier refusal removed on a\n    65\t   copy:\n    66\t   - Q1 + Q2 Data Center revenue = \"FY2027 first half\" is refused, because the period parser reads only `H1`.\n    67\t   - FY2026 Q4 × (1 + the source's stated 65% year-over-year growth) is refused for want of a bridge. The check excuses\n    68\t     `apply_growth` only under a family `same_base` relation.\n    69\t   - $411 billion × 92.5% is computed by `product` as 38,017.5.\n    70\t   - \"well over $300 billion\" is refused because the parser starts one word later.\n    71\t   - $1.05 trillion is compared with bands in billions.\n    72\t3. **Model errors seen in the sample:**\n    73\t   - a 15% growth rate supported by forecasts computed from that same rate, a cycle;\n    74\t   - $25 billion and $18 billion of commitments added, although the source does not establish that the $18 billion comes on top of\n    75\t     the $25 billion;\n    76\t   - a full-year residual taken as a forecast. This is a judgement for a reader, not for code.\n    77\t4. **Diagnostic on copies (Claude's script, labelled a probe, not a count of right answers).**\n    78\t   - The script mechanically corrected the format classes.\n    79\t   - Result: 25 of 36 first attempts passed the early structure check, 9 had no structure error at all, and 0 would publish. The\n    80\t     retries gave the same counts.\n    81\t   - It guesses links from matching amounts, so it does not show how many answers a repaired request would get right.\n    82\t\n    83\t## 3. Process error\n    84\t\n    85\tAGENTS §6 says: \"Check before the send, at no cost. Write one answer that follows the prompt and run every code check on it.\"\n    86\t\n    87\t- **What the $0 gate proved.** Its passing answer, like the rehearsal's clean fixture, was written by someone who knew the check's\n    88\t  ids, units and period spellings. It proved that the harness accepts a conforming answer, not that the request teaches one.\n    89\t- **The missed step.** A writer who sees only the outgoing request writes the answer, and that first output goes through the real\n    90\t  checks. Each refusal must then point to the sentence of the request that states its rule.\n    91\t- **What the eight council rounds covered.** Rounds 47 to 47h reviewed the harness. None read the request as the model reads it\n    92\t  against the check.\n    93\t- **A wrong field in the mid-run diagnosis.** Claude told Alex the prose sat in `rests_on`. It sat in `evidence`, `bridge`, `outcome`\n    94\t  and `reference`.\n    95\t\n    96\t## 4. Council consensus: one recommendation, one test (for Alex's choice)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md:43:**Not one of the 90 member answers named a figure as its outcome**, in either journal. This failure alone refuses every answer.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:76:  - Compare the paid gate (D733), where 0 of 90 outcomes named a figure.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport importlib.util,json,re,copy\nbase=Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'')\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('\\\\''blind_test'\\\\'',base/'\\\\''blind_test.py'\\\\'')\nb=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(b)\ncs=b.cs\np=Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22'\\\\'')\nrows=json.loads((p/'\\\\''CHECKED.json'\\\\'').read_text())\ntransition=re.compile(r'\\\\''\\\\b(?:grow|rise|fall|increase|decrease|decline|shrink)\\\\b[\"'^.!?]*?'\"\\\\bbetween\\\\s+(?:this year|\\\\d{4})\\\\s+and\\\\s+(?:this year|\\\\d{4})\\\\s*,\\\\s*from\\\\s*\"'$'\"'\\\\'',re.I)\ndef trial_expressions(text):\n    spans=[]\n    for form,rx in cs._SCAN:\n        for m in rx.finditer(text):\n            if form in ('\\\\''range'\\\\'','\\\\''percent_range'\\\\'') and re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\bto\\\\b'\\\\'',m[0],re.I) and transition.search(text[:m.start()]):\n                continue\n            if not any(m.start()<hi and lo<m.end() for lo,hi in spans):\n                spans.append(m.span())\n    return sorted(spans)\ncs.expressions=trial_expressions\nchanges=[]\nfor row in rows:\n    d=p/row['\\\\''case'\\\\'']; it=json.loads((d/'\\\\''item.json'\\\\'').read_text()); a=json.loads((d/'\\\\''answers'\\\\''/f\\\"{row['\\\\''writer'\\\\'']}.json\\\").read_text())\n    ca=cs.from_answer(a,it['\\\\''family'\\\\'']); z=cs.check(it['\\\\''family'\\\\''],it['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],ca)\n    if json.loads(json.dumps(z))\"'!={k:row[k] for k in ('\"'\\\\''errors'\\\\'','\\\\''published'\\\\'','\\\\''recorded'\\\\'')}:\n        changes.append((row['\\\\''case'\\\\''],row['\\\\''writer'\\\\''],z['\\\\''errors'\\\\''],z['\\\\''published'\\\\'']))\n    if row['\\\\''case'\\\\'']=='\\\\''E'\\\\'' and row['\\\\''writer'\\\\'']=='\\\\''claude'\\\\'':\n        f=next(f for f in ca['\\\\''figures'\\\\''] if f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']=='\\\\''F4'\\\\'')\n        for num,value,low,high in [('\\\\''\"'$170 billion'\"'\\\\'',170,None,None),('\\\\''\"'$35 billion to $170 billion'\"'\\\\'',None,35,170)]:\n            cf={k:v for k,v in dict(f,quote_number=num,value=value,low=low,high=high).items() if v is not None}\n            print(num,cs._sources(it['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],{'\\\\''F4'\\\\'':cf}))\nprint('\\\\''In-memory split changes:'\\\\'',changes)\nfor txt in ['\\\\''Guidance ranges from \"'$195 billion to $205 billion.'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''A range of \"'$195 billion to $205 billion.'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Sales of \"'$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''The share is between 72% and 73%.'\\\\'']:\n    print(txt,[txt[i:j] for i,j in cs.expressions(txt)])\nfor f in ('\\\\''answers'\\\\'','\\\\''retries'\\\\''):\n    rows=[json.loads(x) for x in (Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22'\\\\'')/(f+'\\\\''.jsonl'\\\\'')).read_text().splitlines()]\n    print(f,len(rows),list(rows[0]))\n    print({k:type(v).__name__ for k,v in rows[0].items()})\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport importlib.util,json,re,copy\nbase=Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'')\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('\\\\''blind_test'\\\\'',base/'\\\\''blind_test.py'\\\\'')\nb=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(b)\ncs=b.cs\np=Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22'\\\\'')\nrows=json.loads((p/'\\\\''CHECKED.json'\\\\'').read_text())\ntransition=re.compile(r'\\\\''\\\\b(?:grow|rise|fall|increase|decrease|decline|shrink)\\\\b[\"'^.!?]*?'\"\\\\bbetween\\\\s+(?:this year|\\\\d{4})\\\\s+and\\\\s+(?:this year|\\\\d{4})\\\\s*,\\\\s*from\\\\s*\"'$'\"'\\\\'',re.I)\ndef trial_expressions(text):\n    spans=[]\n    for form,rx in cs._SCAN:\n        for m in rx.finditer(text):\n            if form in ('\\\\''range'\\\\'','\\\\''percent_range'\\\\'') and re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\bto\\\\b'\\\\'',m[0],re.I) and transition.search(text[:m.start()]):\n                continue\n            if not any(m.start()<hi and lo<m.end() for lo,hi in spans):\n                spans.append(m.span())\n    return sorted(spans)\ncs.expressions=trial_expressions\nchanges=[]\nfor row in rows:\n    d=p/row['\\\\''case'\\\\'']; it=json.loads((d/'\\\\''item.json'\\\\'').read_text()); a=json.loads((d/'\\\\''answers'\\\\''/f\\\"{row['\\\\''writer'\\\\'']}.json\\\").read_text())\n    ca=cs.from_answer(a,it['\\\\''family'\\\\'']); z=cs.check(it['\\\\''family'\\\\''],it['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],ca)\n    if json.loads(json.dumps(z))\"'!={k:row[k] for k in ('\"'\\\\''errors'\\\\'','\\\\''published'\\\\'','\\\\''recorded'\\\\'')}:\n        changes.append((row['\\\\''case'\\\\''],row['\\\\''writer'\\\\''],z['\\\\''errors'\\\\''],z['\\\\''published'\\\\'']))\n    if row['\\\\''case'\\\\'']=='\\\\''E'\\\\'' and row['\\\\''writer'\\\\'']=='\\\\''claude'\\\\'':\n        f=next(f for f in ca['\\\\''figures'\\\\''] if f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']=='\\\\''F4'\\\\'')\n        for num,value,low,high in [('\\\\''\"'$170 billion'\"'\\\\'',170,None,None),('\\\\''\"'$35 billion to $170 billion'\"'\\\\'',None,35,170)]:\n            cf={k:v for k,v in dict(f,quote_number=num,value=value,low=low,high=high).items() if v is not None}\n            print(num,cs._sources(it['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],{'\\\\''F4'\\\\'':cf}))\nprint('\\\\''In-memory split changes:'\\\\'',changes)\nfor txt in ['\\\\''Guidance ranges from \"'$195 billion to $205 billion.'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''A range of \"'$195 billion to $205 billion.'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Sales of \"'$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''The share is between 72% and 73%.'\\\\'']:\n    print(txt,[txt[i:j] for i,j in cs.expressions(txt)])\nfor f in ('\\\\''answers'\\\\'','\\\\''retries'\\\\''):\n    rows=[json.loads(x) for x in (Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22'\\\\'')/(f+'\\\\''.jsonl'\\\\'')).read_text().splitlines()]\n    print(f,len(rows),list(rows[0]))\n    print({k:type(v).__name__ for k,v in rows[0].items()})\n'\"","aggregated_output":"$170 billion []\n$35 billion to $170 billion [('S1', 'F4: \"$35 billion to $170 billion\" is not written in the quote of e4857 as a complete number')]\nIn-memory split changes: [('E', 'claude', [], {'v41': [34.0, 34.0, None]})]\nGuidance ranges from $195 billion to $205 billion. ['$195 billion to $205 billion']\nA range of $195 billion to $205 billion. ['$195 billion to $205 billion']\nSales of $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. ['$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%']\nThe share is between 72% and 73%. ['between 72% and 73%']\nanswers 72 ['unit', 'arm', 'draw', 'attempt', 'request_sha256', 'status']\n{'unit': 'str', 'arm': 'str', 'draw': 'int', 'attempt': 'int', 'request_sha256': 'str', 'status': 'str'}\nretries 72 ['unit', 'arm', 'draw', 'attempt', 'request_sha256', 'status']\n{'unit': 'str', 'arm': 'str', 'draw': 'int', 'attempt': 'int', 'request_sha256': 'str', 'status': 'str'}\n"