{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|D73[7-9]'\"' docs/DECISIONS.md | tail -n 20; rg -n 'Q4 |R0[568]|R12' poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/reader-packets/R12.claude.json | cut -c 1-850\"","aggregated_output":"91:## Latest decision: return complete evidence without the 1 MB rejection (D376)\n95:## Latest decision: return the full question catalog without the 150 KB rejection (D377)\n99:## 2. Research universe (PRD 01)\n110:## 3. Classification (PRD 02)\n120:## 4. Config (PRD 03)\n129:## 5. Dispatch (PRD 04)\n137:## 6. Extraction (PRD 05 and the extraction standard)\n172:## 7. Thesis library (PRD 06)\n239:## 8. Closing and pull mode (PRD 07, PRD 08)\n251:## 9. Review pool (PRD 09)\n257:## 10. Current phase: filing that links facts the way an analyst does (PRD 10)\n294:## 12. Idea API and service (docs/poc/idea-card.md, docs/poc/service.md)\n312:## 13. Data (README, \"Local requirements and data\")\n320:## 14. Operations (README, AGENTS §9)\n332:## 15. Working rules (AGENTS.md)\n340:## Index\n1079:| D735 | 2026-11-22 | (superseded by D737) Council 49–50: the v13 repair is finished to a line (at most two more review rounds: wording and cases, then the sent request and checks; then the blind test once; a serious issue after the second goes back to Alex); shrinking to six checks set aside (drops C8's segment-into-total guard; exceeds D734); design v2 | superseded by D737 | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md` |\n1081:| D737 | 2026-11-22 | Alex: shrink judging-v13's format — code refuses only five defects (number misread, wrong arithmetic, part above or added into its whole, two forecasts of one quarter, own estimate as the market's) and broken structure, each rule in one or two sentences beside its field; the rest shown to readers; council within that scope; then the $0 blind test; supersedes D735's full restatement | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n1082:| D738 | 2026-11-22 | v13s build rule (council 52–53): code refuses a named defect only where the calculation's structure decides it (direct part+whole sum, two forecast-basis figures or a bypassed shared forecast, part above whole on recomputed values, estimate/forecast at or under the reference, plus S1/S2/S6/S7); indirect forms recorded for readers, who mark the five defects on every reply (an accepted reply with a reader-marked defect stops the blind test); round 53's false refusals fixed | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md` |\n1083:| D739 | 2026-11-22 | v13s built: council 54 fixes (whole-expression sources, values over ranged leaves, linked part/whole, period-aware S8, adopted forecasts only, stricter structure, a hardened blind runner); cases 100/100, mutants 38/38, rehearsal 19/19, old harness unchanged; the blind test runs now and its result goes to Council B | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md` |\n1:{\"members\": {\"v8\": {\"supported\": \"yes\", \"ground\": \"H1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of 164.25 is F1 (e109, 75.25) plus F2 (e2650, 89.0), which matches e5309's $164bn. The Q3 company revenue estimate F10 of 112.5 sits between guidance F8 (e2652, 108 +/-2%) and the outside estimate F9 (e5056, roughly 113.6). Its stated basis is the prior-quarter beat (e3200), Rubin shipments (e2693), CoreWeave's deployment (e5118) and the supply cap (e5067). The Q4 assumption F12 is 13% sequential growth, the guided Q3 pace F11 (108/96.2-1 = 12.27%) plus a small increase grounded on e3406 and limited by e5067 and e5205; it gives F13 = 127.125. The H2 Data Center share F15 is 93%, slightly above the Q2 share F5 (89/96.2 = 92.5%), grounded on e5061, e5223 and e3406 and consistent with the rising share in e3399. H2 Data Center F16 = 239.625 x 0.93 = 222.85. The\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
